            <ArticleTitle>Simple method for cardioplegia retrieval in patients with chronic renal failure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1240-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case in which a retrograde cardioplegia catheter was inserted into the coronary sinus for retrieval of antegrade cardioplegia in a patient with chronic renal failure is described. Potassium levels were maintained within normal limits throughout the procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
